{"name":"English Saddle","hex":"#8e6947","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"english","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spinning or rotary motion given to a ball around the vertical axis, as in pool, billiards or bowling; spin, sidespin.","An unusual or unexpected interpretation of a text or idea, a spin, a nuance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/english"},{"term":"saddle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seat for a rider, typically made of leather and raised in the front and rear, placed on the back of a horse or other animal, and secured by a strap around the animal's body.\n\nA similar implement used to secure goods to animals; a packsaddle.\nSynonym of harness saddle (“the part of a harness which supports the weight of poles or shafts attaching a vehicle to a horse or other animal”).\nA cushion used as a seat in a cart or other vehicle.\nThe immovable seat of a bicycle, motorcycle, or similar vehicle.\n\nChiefly preceded by the: horse-riding as an activity or occupation.\n\nSynonym of saddle brown (“a medium brown colour, like that of saddle leather”).","A similar implement used to secure goods to animals; a packsaddle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put a saddle (noun sense 1) on (an animal).\n\nTo put (something) on to another thing like a saddle on an animal.\n\n\nTo enter (a trained horse) into a race.\n Chiefly followed by with: to burden or encumber (someone) with some problem or responsibility.","To put a saddle (noun sense 1) on (an animal)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saddle"}],"entries":[{"title":"English saddle","blocks":[{"text":"English saddles are saddles used to ride horses in English riding disciplines throughout the world. The discipline is not limited to England, the United Kingdom in general or other English-speaking countries. This style of saddle is used in all of the Olympic and International Federation for Equestrian Sports (FEI) equestrian disciplines, except for the newly approved FEI events of equestrian vaulting and reining. Most designs were specifically developed to allow the horse freedom of movement, whether jumping, running, or moving quickly across rugged, broken country with fences. Unlike the western saddle or Australian Stock Saddle, there is no horn or other design elements that stick out above the main tree of the saddle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Lipizzaner_DSC02439.jpg/330px-Lipizzaner_DSC02439.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_saddle","wikidata":"Q3954915"},{"title":"Saddle","blocks":[{"text":"A saddle is a supportive structure for a rider of an animal, fastened to an animal's back by a girth. The most common type is equestrian. However, specialized saddles have been created for oxen, camels and other animals. The trade of making saddles is saddlery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Saddle_with_shabrack_according_to_tradition_linked_with_Hetman_Miko%C5%82aj_Hieronim_Sieniawski.jpg/330px-Saddle_with_shabrack_according_to_tradition_linked_with_Hetman_Miko%C5%82aj_Hieronim_Sieniawski.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saddle","wikidata":"Q192249"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/EnglishSaddleParts.png/500px-EnglishSaddleParts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/EnglishSaddleParts.png/500px-EnglishSaddleParts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parts of an English Saddle (All-Purpose style)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnglishSaddleParts.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/NakedSaddle%21.jpg/500px-NakedSaddle%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/NakedSaddle%21.jpg/500px-NakedSaddle%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A saddle with most leather removed, showing tree and seat padding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANakedSaddle!.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/SaddleUnderside.jpg/500px-SaddleUnderside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/SaddleUnderside.jpg/1280px-SaddleUnderside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/SaddleUnderside.jpg/500px-SaddleUnderside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Underside of a Dressage saddle, showing panels, gullet, sweat flaps and tips of the billets","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaddleUnderside.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/SpringTreeStructure.jpg/500px-SpringTreeStructure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/SpringTreeStructure.jpg/500px-SpringTreeStructure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stripped-down saddle, showing spring tree structure that underlies the panels","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpringTreeStructure.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/SaddleBillets.jpg/500px-SaddleBillets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/SaddleBillets.jpg/1280px-SaddleBillets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/SaddleBillets.jpg/500px-SaddleBillets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Billets, sweat flap, buckle guard, and knee rolls. These are under the flap of the saddle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaddleBillets.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg/500px-Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg/1280px-Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg/500px-Franz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The traditional hunting saddle, with a low pommel and cantle, and no padding. Note the long stirrup and the rider's seat, his feet pushed forward, which was the common position of the time.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFranz_Kr%C3%BCger_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/WesternSaddle2.jpg/250px-WesternSaddle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/WesternSaddle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/WesternSaddle2.jpg/250px-WesternSaddle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A western saddle. Note the lack of panels and addition of prominent pommels and cantle, the difference in stirrups, and the traditional horn.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWesternSaddle2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/CollegiateEventer.jpg/500px-CollegiateEventer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/CollegiateEventer.jpg/500px-CollegiateEventer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"All-purpose or eventing saddle, crossing a deeper seat and long flap with a more forward flap placement.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACollegiateEventer.jpg"}],"sounds":{"english":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/En-us-english.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/13/En-us-english.ogg/En-us-english.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/En-uk-English.oga?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2d/En-uk-English.oga/En-uk-English.oga.mp3"}],"saddle":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3e/En-us-saddle.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3e/En-us-saddle.ogg/En-us-saddle.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Vase with lamps, Brown and beige textures, Rostov-on-Don, Russia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/500px-Vase_with_lamps%2C_Brown_and_beige_textures%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg","ratio":1.5049019607843137,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vase_with_lamps,_Brown_and_beige_textures,_Rostov-on-Don,_Russ